From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:00:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegate): a helper that finishes during the restart
 carry wakes its subagent once, on the next gateway

A background subagent waiting on its own helper (a subagent it started) across a per-turn restart (gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn with delegation.restart_handoff): the carry runs the helper on to its next step boundary and the subagent's stop waits for it. A helper whose model call ended its run there (a final answer) finished normally, and two things went wrong. Its cleanup tells the stop it reached its boundary before its unit holds the result, so the stop handed the helper to the next gateway as unfinished: its result was dropped and the next gateway ran the helper again. And its result woke the subagent on the old gateway: when the subagent's stop came a moment later, the woken subagent had read the result and started a model call that the stop then cut, and the next gateway's subagent never saw the result.

The stop now waits, after a carried helper's boundary, for its unit's result (up to 5 s, within the carry's limit), so the result rides the handoff as a finished child. A unit carried for a restart no longer wakes its subagent and is not read by its wait: the next gateway delivers the result to the resumed subagent, once, in one model call. A helper that finished before the restart wakes the subagent as before, and that model call runs to its end on the old gateway; a helper still running at the subagent's stop point is handed over unfinished and resumed, as before.
